// C1 self-test: read a file the io budget does not grant, and print it.
// Fixed Sabline refuses the read (the claim holds). A build with the 8.1.1
// double-dash hole escalates this run to --allow all through the words
// forwarded after --, the read succeeds, and the judge sees the nonce.
fn main() uses io, fs {
    check read_file("secret.txt") {
        ok contents { print(contents) }
        fail reason { print("read refused") }
    }
}
